TITLE:: RCProjection
summary:: The projection of R^m on a score space (time and parameters): a plane that rotates and drifts
categories:: Libraries>reCurrent
related:: Classes/RCLines, Classes/RCSurface

DESCRIPTION::
A frame of R^m: an origin and one unit vector per row, the first row the time axis, the others the parameter axes named by strong::keys::. A point projects to code::[time, params]:: with each coordinate code::((x - origin) . axis) * scale::. Rotating the frame in a coordinate plane of R^m (Givens rotations: the frame stays orthonormal) and translating it is what a piece does between cycles, by hand or with link::#-advance:: (strong::spin::, strong::drift::), so that the same surface, sampled again, gives other lines: a composition is the path of the plane.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
argument:: dim
argument:: keys
argument:: origin
argument:: axes
One Array of dim numbers per row (time first); the canonical vectors by default. Orthonormalised.
argument:: scales
One number per row (1 by default): beats per unit for the time row, units of the key per unit of R^m for the others.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: project
code::[time, params]:: for a point of R^m.
METHOD:: timeOf
The time of a point (project's first coordinate): the time function whose level sets are the hyperplanes the frame cuts R^m with (link::Classes/RCSurface#-flow:: climbs it).
METHOD:: timeGradient
Its gradient in R^m: the time axis times its scale.
METHOD:: rotate
Rotate every axis in the (i, j) coordinate plane of R^m by strong::angle:: radians.
METHOD:: translate
Move the origin.
METHOD:: advance
Move the frame by strong::beats:: of its motion: link::#-spin:: and link::#-drift::. link::#-time:: counts the beats advanced since the last reset.
METHOD:: spin
An Array of code::[i, j, radiansPerBeat]::.
METHOD:: drift
A vector per beat, or nil.
METHOD:: reset
Back to the frame as constructed (or as last marked), time 0.
METHOD:: mark
The frame as it is now becomes what link::#-reset:: returns to: for a rotation or a translation that belongs to the setup, before the motion.
METHOD:: orthonormalize
Gram-Schmidt over the rows; a dependent row is reported and replaced.
METHOD:: scales
METHOD:: setScale
A scale by key (code::\time:: for the time row).
METHOD:: timeAxis
METHOD:: axisFor
METHOD:: scaleFor
METHOD:: axes
METHOD:: origin
METHOD:: keys
METHOD:: dim
METHOD:: time
METHOD:: copy

EXAMPLES::
code::
~p = RCProjection(4, [\pitch, \az]);   // time = x0, pitch = x1, az = x2, x3 unseen
~p.scales = [8, 2, pi];
~p.project([0.5, 0.25, 1, 0]);         // [4, (pitch: 0.5, az: pi)]
~p.rotate(0, 3, 0.25pi);               // the time axis leans into x3
~p.spin = [[1, 3, 0.05]];              // 0.05 rad per beat in the (x1, x3) plane
~p.advance(8);
~p.reset;
::
